    Fix three soundness bugs in BV encoding (fo-farmland, fo-sailing)
    
    1. getEffStepRules (PDDL2SMTBV): called fromPddl without bv=True for
       non-simple linear increment effects. Mixed BV/Real types hit the
       except:pass in __binary, leaving aux variables unconstrained.
       Solver then assigned phantom resource values.
    
    2. fromPddl * operator (SMTExpression): multiplying two already-scaled
       BV values gave a scale_factor^2 result. Added BVUDiv by scale_factor
       after every * in BV mode to compensate.
    
    3. BVMul ITE optimization (__binary): replaced v*k with
       Ite(v>0, k, 0), which is only correct for binary (0/1) action
       counts, not for state variables like velocity. Replaced with
       BVMul for all non-trivial cases.
    
    4. main_bv.py loop: always broke after finding any plan, even invalid
       ones. Now only breaks when isValid=True so higher bounds are tried.
    
